ted","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"kai\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"reuse\\\",\\\"ability\\\":\\\"probe\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Reuse the existing general observation/sample-interaction operation as a non-ingestive assessment precursor. Its observe mode directly supports examining the actual sample without assuming nutrition or toxicity knowledge. The related eat, gather, consult, exchange and food-air-exposure-trial capabilities were also checked in the supplied retrievals. None supplies a validated toxicity assay or nutritional measurement: eating causes real exposure, and air exposure measures decay rather than safety. With the known equipment and evidence, nutrition and toxicity cannot be established reliably. This meets the request's explicit fallback without inventing a safe tasting test or a new duplicate observation capability.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Reference: probe, equivalence open-baseline:probe:1, handler open.probe, revision foundation-open@1. Use its existing parameters target, mode and intensity; do not add an ingestion or assay mode. General applicability: any actor may observe an accessible visible subject or perform an already supported physical interaction on an applicable owned sample. For this applicant, first resolve the actual visible, reachable sample item-16-kai-164, an already-owned quantity-1 hazelnut stack from start-1-nuts harvested at tick 16. No new gathering is necessary; the older intention to gather is superseded by the supplied inventory. Ownership alone does not establish current reach. If unreachable, movement is a separate action with its own costs. Execute mode observe with intensity 0, using the exact resolved sample reference as target. Preconditions and reference validity must pass before charging or reporting completion. Cost: one simulation round and 0.2 energy for a completed observation, plus ordinary world metabolism during that round. No food, water, tool, fuel or comparison berry is consumed, created or transferred. The sample retains its actual quantity and continues ordinary decay; observation does not preserve it. Report only observable features actually returned by the handler, with subject, tick, method and evidence-event reference. Distinguish observation from inference; if no diagnostic feature is observable, report that limitation rather than manufacturing a finding. The known berry nutrition 8 and toxicity 0 are prior personal knowledge, not measurements of this hazelnut and not a calibration that transfers to it. Optional separate observation of item-4-kai-36 costs another round and 0.2 energy and can compare only observable features. Do not disclose hidden hazelnut nutrition, toxicity, composition or safety fields. Appearance, maturity, lack of visible damage, and an absence of immediate symptoms do not establish safety. No ingestion, mouth-contact test, heating, wetting, shell opening or laboratory assay is included. Physical probe modes cost 0.5 energy and 0.1 actual material unit per existing contract and may be used only where their real prerequisites and implemented effects are supported; they are not toxicity tests. Eat remains a separate operation, with minimum quantity 1 under its existing schema, one round, 1 energy, actual food consumption and actual nutrition/toxicity effects. It must not be silently used as a fractional low-risk trial: unknown exposure risk cannot be bounded here, health 100 does not establish tolerance, food does not directly heal, and the berry reserve is not an antidote. No controlled exposure is prescribed. Work follows probe's existing one-complete-interaction, cancel-on-interruption execution rule; incomplete observation yields no completed finding or success event. There is no partial-work credit to resume; a later attempt is a new paid interaction. Cancellation or death stops pending work, with no delayed observation or duplicated effect; unspent resources remain with their actual owner, incurred time/effort is not refunded, and no sample escrow is needed for observe mode. Global pauses preserve execution state under existing rules. No ongoing assessment process or maintenance is created. Real output is only the performed observation and its actual evidence, not nutrition knowledge, a safety certificate, inventory or mastery. Review waiting does not advance the world.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":0,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"The request, review, naming, consultation and any learning or registration award nothing. A completed observation may qualify only if its event verifies a personally relevant information gain, including a genuinely informative inability to discriminate; merely printing 'unknown' or repeating the same query is not a new discovery. Apply the established experience rules in code, not by repeated model judgment: deduplicate by functional subject/property/evidence, require a real event, and use existing bounded caps, decay and cooldowns. Familiar legitimate investigation may support only the existing modest maintained benefit when real participation occurs. Do not create a new reward amount where none is established, grant novelty bonuses for renamed tests, or change protected reward accounts, budget, goals or permissions. No automatic pleasure, satisfaction, physical comfort, healing or satiety is conferred. Physical comfort remains capped at 10, and mood never reduces basic nutrition.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse the existing probe interaction and the sample's actual visual representation. Any observation cue must be driven by a real start/completion/interruption event and reusable metadata identifying the actor, resolved target, mode, tick, phase and evidence reference. Reuse existing rendering/event code and record those dependencies rather than claiming reinvention. Completed observation may display 'observed; nutrition/toxicity undetermined' only when supported by its event. Do not show a safety badge, numeric nutritional reading, toxin warning based on hidden state, laboratory apparatus, eating animation or altered sample appearance without the corresponding real effect. Failure and interruption must remain visibly incomplete or failed, never successful. Visual feedback is separate from functional results and experience eligibility.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"bfb2bd85-9fd3-4022-9b6f-e9b14ac8f962","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4902,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens_details":{"ttl_30m_tokens":0,"ttl_12h_tokens":0}},"output_tokens":1354,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":198},"total_tokens":6256,"attribution":{"items":{"msg_0e13f90584c345af016b089ba9ffb887d1886bf7b49eb2234f":{"input_tokens":4141,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":4141,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_to